    "created_at": "2015-09-21T15:15:10Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-09-21T15:15:10Z",
    "body": "To be pendantic, \"soft\" is in the same situation as \"off\" when it comes to form submission, namely that it isn't one of the strings \"physical\", \"hard\" or \"on\" that trigger the `valueWithHardLineBreaks()` code path.\n\nIt seems to me that it would be simpler to describe this attribute in a single place and not bother trying to single out the non-conforming values, but that's less important than getting interop on the actual behavior, of course.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
